  "body": "The house is vacant. Immediate possession is available. \r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned on the seaward side of Ngapipi Road, this is one of only nine privileged residences occupying this remarkably rare waterfront position. Behind its discreet street presence lies an architecturally designed home capturing breathtaking panoramic views across the Orakei Basin to Auckland’s glittering city skyline.\r\n\r\nFrom the road, you would never imagine what awaits beyond the gates. Step inside and an entirely different world unfolds — a private waterfront sanctuary offering a sense of space, tranquillity and connection to the water that few Auckland homes can match.\r\n\r\nSet on 1,158sqm (approx.) of prime freehold land with approximately 326sqm (approx.) of versatile living, the residence has been thoughtfully positioned so every bedroom and principal living space embraces the waterfront outlook. From peaceful morning reflections across the Basin to spectacular sunsets and the city lights illuminating the skyline after dark, the view is constantly changing and endlessly captivating.\r\n\r\nDespite the feeling of waterfront seclusion, this exceptional property remains remarkably connected to the city. Orakei Bay Village, Eastridge Shopping Centre and the Coates Avenue shops are all close by, while convenient motorway connections and public transport put Auckland CBD within easy reach. The property is zoned for Orakei School and Selwyn College, with the beaches and lifestyle attractions of the Eastern Bays only minutes away.\r\n\r\nAdding further value to this special setting is Te Ara ki Uta ki Tai, the waterfront connection around the Orakei Basin. Positioned in front of the property yet naturally screened by established native trees, the coastal pathway further enhances access to one of Auckland’s most beautiful environments for walking, running and cycling.\r\n\r\nOpportunities to secure substantial freehold land directly on the Orakei Basin are exceptionally rare.\r\n\r\nPrivate viewing is available by appointment.\r\n\r\nFor agents: Conjunctional sales are welcome and encouraged.",
